{
  "abstract": "For every finite simple connected bridgeless cubic graph G, the survivor can force full zombie damage if and only if G is not isomorphic to K4, K3,3, the triangular prism or the cube. In particular, for order n at least 10 this proves Randy Davila's Conjecture 24, zdmg(G)=n, with an explicit bound of 2n(n+1) survivor moves against every initial zombie position and every legal geodesic reply. The game formalization retains starting and turn order, survivor passes, capture and distinct-vertex damage, and proves the numerical payoff's connection to bounded and eventual strategies. The argument classifies short-cycle components, bounds their boundaries by four ports and composes metric exit and target routes into an ambient-graph strategy. Structural expansion corollaries and recurrent-coverage extensions accompany the characterization. The 39 selected results connect structural cubic-graph theory with extremal damage and worst-case strategies in graph pursuit. All proof sources are included in one Lake project.",
